        <item>
            <title>3.26.0</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:22:52 +0900</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/Saqoosha/Canopy</link>
            <sparkle:version>231</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>3.26.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### Features
- Claude sessions on two paired Macs can now message each other. Run `canopyctl peers` (or ask Claude; the new `remote-peers` skill knows how) to list the sessions on your paired Macs, then send to one with `SendMessage`. Replies come back the same way, labelled with the sending Mac's name. Both Macs need this version and each other's connection in Settings › Remote.

### Known limits
- A message to a session running in a different permission mode may be held for approval, which a Canopy pane cannot show, so it can expire unseen.
- If delivery fails on the other Mac, the sending session is not told.
]]></description>
